Perfect! All tests now pass. 

The bug was a classic off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]` to return the first word. This caused:
1. `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
2. `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError

The fix was simple: change `parts[1]` to `parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split list.
